## 6. Critical Appointment Business Logic

This section is essential.

The booking engine must work reliably.

### Availability

Appointment availability must be calculated using:

- Doctor schedule.
- Working days.
- Schedule exceptions.
- Appointment duration.
- Breaks.
- Existing bookings.
- Configured daily capacity.
- Per-slot capacity.
- Current date and time.
- Temporary appointment holds, where applicable.

Use **Africa/Cairo** as the default timezone, but make it configurable.

Store timestamps consistently and handle conversion between local time and UTC correctly.

Past appointment times must never be bookable.

### Capacity Management

Each doctor should have a configurable daily limit.

Example:

Doctor A has a maximum of 20 appointments per day.

If 19 valid appointments exist, only one additional appointment can be confirmed.

When the 20th appointment is booked, the schedule must stop accepting additional bookings.

If a 21st patient attempts to book, the system must reject the request and offer the waitlist.

For normal one-patient time slots, prevent two patients from booking the same doctor and time.

### Concurrency Protection

Implement atomic booking operations using Firestore transactions or an equivalently safe server-controlled mechanism.

Verify capacity and reserve the appointment atomically.

Protect both daily capacity and individual time slots.

If two users try to reserve the final available appointment simultaneously, only one booking may succeed.

Do not rely on frontend counters or disabled buttons to enforce availability.

### Booking Statuses

Support:

- Confirmed
- Checked In
- Completed
- Cancelled
- No Show

Define status transitions explicitly.

Completed and no-show appointments still count as historical booked capacity for their time period.

Cancelled appointments may release capacity under valid rules.

Prevent duplicate active bookings for the same patient, doctor, and time slot.

### Cancellation

Allow cancellations according to configurable rules.

Default example: patient self-cancellation is permitted until 4 hours before the appointment.

Administrators or authorized receptionists may handle special cases.

Never delete booking history when canceling. Preserve the cancellation status and audit event.

### No-Show Handling

Receptionists can mark patients as absent once an appointment's appropriate check-in period has passed.

Record no-show statistics.

Do not automatically block patients from future appointments based solely on no-show history.

### No External Payment Dependency

The initial application should not require online payment.

Do not implement fake payment processing.

The system must be fully functional without a payment gateway.

### Notifications

Implement real in-app notifications.

For SMS, email, and WhatsApp, show integration readiness or demo simulation only unless a real provider is connected.

Clearly label simulated notifications.

